[{:db/id "q-97720/selection/6afc0d0880e80c79b176ae8470032d6ef13cad5a4f1e8f31e6ac29857fa4414b" :answer/id #uuid "094b1773-13a4-562f-9ff3-8a403fd7b748" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,\\pi )$ and the radius $\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97720/selection/e9ab433515f0b09fb9df468de5e9ce397ea51af78044e201fe00cad2bdfa0544" :answer/id #uuid "3e281020-d66d-5c39-8dda-e11a76cb2d67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius $\\frac{1}{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97720/selection/81036d12e1e0983c6156480596364bb66e20cb367580f9430b209415fba003a9" :answer/id #uuid "cbe3406b-3d23-502c-b08b-0d004b563c64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97720/selection/64e6130a4e1ad37cf26541a6a972bfff1cf70af0e125f0b6c84ae64e2e020976" :answer/id #uuid "5a1b57f2-f166-55db-bc24-a171c453bc82" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97720/selection/2b208cd6d48b37ca70d3e03db82796648f095819a8cb8b4ce466aa1fb4797f51" :answer/id #uuid "177256cf-bb3e-5b88-ab07-5d736af1a6c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,-1)$ and the radius $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97720/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "363911d0-eb2a-5ef2-9599-893a67972d43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97720/selection/81036d12e1e0983c6156480596364bb66e20cb367580f9430b209415fba003a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-97720/selection/6afc0d0880e80c79b176ae8470032d6ef13cad5a4f1e8f31e6ac29857fa4414b" "q-97720/selection/e9ab433515f0b09fb9df468de5e9ce397ea51af78044e201fe00cad2bdfa0544" "q-97720/selection/81036d12e1e0983c6156480596364bb66e20cb367580f9430b209415fba003a9" "q-97720/selection/64e6130a4e1ad37cf26541a6a972bfff1cf70af0e125f0b6c84ae64e2e020976" "q-97720/selection/2b208cd6d48b37ca70d3e03db82796648f095819a8cb8b4ce466aa1fb4797f51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97720" :question/id #uuid "fd2936d9-6a40-5af8-901d-a96142d64a90" :question/math-academy-id "q-97720" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,4)$ where $t=1,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖=3\\pi ,$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t),$ we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(1)=⟨0,4⟩,$  since the point $P(0,4)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t),$ ${T}^{′}(1)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(1)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2}),-\\pi t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi {t}^{2}}{2})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =⟨-\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩=⟨0,-\\pi ⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-\\pi )^{2}}=\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{3\\pi }{\\pi }=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=1$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }⟨0,-\\pi ⟩=⟨0,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1)+R(1)N(1) & =⟨0,4⟩+3⟨0,-1⟩=⟨0,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97720/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132125/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9c3a7380-8a7b-5249-b9e9-f762c93c0c75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132125/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "a2dbdd45-cc28-5675-9466-5c39a85615ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132125/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ba6b8384-d8db-5e10-a3c0-f45c29f6d903" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132125/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "33a848c4-124c-5c97-a276-b2b3c10ef78b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132125/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "af59fb76-438f-5a8b-a629-65029671bc95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132125/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a39f22d2-09d6-5ba2-b65e-57d3438ae6e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132125/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-132125/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-132125/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-132125/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-132125/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-132125/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132125" :question/id #uuid "6760ac8d-6b9d-57a0-830e-36a645310793" :question/math-academy-id "q-132125" :question/problem "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=0$ for the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨1,\\,-{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{-t}⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{-0}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(0)$ and ${r}^{″}(0)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2})^{3}}{1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132125/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a053eb10-be16-5423-9b7b-c23677bb6335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132125"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132129/selection/bff60f2d36afeb7746be2bb06ba7a3c96ceb4677d80cc581576a4f38f18031c5" :answer/id #uuid "0118fbaa-d4cf-5fab-a532-5966df9538f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{\\pi }}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132129/selection/366bdf0be195670ebde865116548c219bf6dfacca04801570d2f39d03f73ce5f" :answer/id #uuid "b97da160-c3cb-56c6-8ca1-52543b94f7f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi }}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132129/selection/92fb14ecf557277180226d1c11190204f548839191b21d3702b98fe7769e212d" :answer/id #uuid "eab75d75-e963-598a-8849-7c24495fecdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132129/selection/6c54ce59f6fd612dcb7ea5a747b709aac7d3fd750f3e30f7d0437a1bb56fe5c2" :answer/id #uuid "fac2f82e-26a4-59c0-9b00-4f8c2d5a9620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-\\pi }}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132129/selection/34d68e4295f5536e87d3ea713ba3332fc6b9f89229b78e1ee04a33fb03f128bc" :answer/id #uuid "5e16b62f-5545-5fba-822b-7bd4263b310e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132129/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e95326b-1972-509c-bd41-38bbe4ef360d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132129/selection/92fb14ecf557277180226d1c11190204f548839191b21d3702b98fe7769e212d" :answer-field/choices ["q-132129/selection/bff60f2d36afeb7746be2bb06ba7a3c96ceb4677d80cc581576a4f38f18031c5" "q-132129/selection/366bdf0be195670ebde865116548c219bf6dfacca04801570d2f39d03f73ce5f" "q-132129/selection/92fb14ecf557277180226d1c11190204f548839191b21d3702b98fe7769e212d" "q-132129/selection/6c54ce59f6fd612dcb7ea5a747b709aac7d3fd750f3e30f7d0437a1bb56fe5c2" "q-132129/selection/34d68e4295f5536e87d3ea713ba3332fc6b9f89229b78e1ee04a33fb03f128bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132129" :question/id #uuid "a402dcc4-c7d6-5188-8327-7ca541f9ca6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132129" :question/problem "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=\\pi $ for the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{-t}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & ={e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2{e}^{-t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-t}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi )$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{-\\pi }⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times 2{e}^{-\\pi }⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =2{e}^{-2\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{({e}^{-\\pi }\\sqrt{2})^{3}}{2{e}^{-2\\pi }} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-3\\pi }}{2{e}^{-2\\pi }} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{-\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132129/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a053eb10-be16-5423-9b7b-c23677bb6335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132129"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132194/selection/9853e3f8fdc4e94c7ad1d4df796acb0bb48377d4b2f33b08aef0b1dfd99ae52e" :answer/id #uuid "0f815760-6fc5-5512-a25f-34a540ec0c4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-\\frac{7}{2},\\frac{11}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132194/selection/b896b3fdaed71f5e7a2dc5ba41c84946f04a7c9f75abdf08319a549260158cd9" :answer/id #uuid "0f2ccf07-e826-5ce8-9d45-b0de19f4784b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨\\frac{15}{2},-\\frac{11}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132194/selection/af8e932007ec92b46a1200abc22ae0a4b88da7a5eb1993b8435131a9573ffb0e" :answer/id #uuid "2109d707-b84a-5aee-862e-b91be0540ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{7}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13}{6}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132194/selection/5a8955c61ebea5d85d41e2f00c43c3120b7f1ba320b9697fa4acbaad6339929d" :answer/id #uuid "a481cc01-f6cb-583a-9add-f8d92b6f9f86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨\\frac{13}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132194/selection/53354928864516e5726bd73b512ac92b917f353215e83d675fe872e5b0d16570" :answer/id #uuid "d4b9007a-f91c-5fab-82ec-61ca36d5ea10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-\\frac{11}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩$ and the radius is $\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132194/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7b6cb4-3e04-5b4c-825c-3eb818e4f343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132194/selection/53354928864516e5726bd73b512ac92b917f353215e83d675fe872e5b0d16570" :answer-field/choices ["q-132194/selection/9853e3f8fdc4e94c7ad1d4df796acb0bb48377d4b2f33b08aef0b1dfd99ae52e" "q-132194/selection/b896b3fdaed71f5e7a2dc5ba41c84946f04a7c9f75abdf08319a549260158cd9" "q-132194/selection/af8e932007ec92b46a1200abc22ae0a4b88da7a5eb1993b8435131a9573ffb0e" "q-132194/selection/5a8955c61ebea5d85d41e2f00c43c3120b7f1ba320b9697fa4acbaad6339929d" "q-132194/selection/53354928864516e5726bd73b512ac92b917f353215e83d675fe872e5b0d16570"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132194" :question/id #uuid "45bddeff-8807-5684-8070-dc3abab32e36" :question/math-academy-id "q-132194" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(1,-1)$ where $t=1,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖=\\sqrt{13},$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}},\\,-\\frac{3t}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(1)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(1)=⟨1,-1⟩,$ since the point $P(1,-1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(1)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(1)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3t}{\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}+4}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{18t}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}},\\,-\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{(9{t}^{2}+4)}^{3}}}⟨-3t,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{{(9({1}^{2})+4)}^{3}}}⟨-3(1),-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot \\sqrt{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{(\\frac{6}{13})} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=1$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1)+R(1)N(1) & =⟨1,-1⟩+\\frac{13\\sqrt{13}}{6}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1⟩+\\frac{13}{6}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1⟩+⟨-\\frac{13}{2},-\\frac{13}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{11}{2},-\\frac{16}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132194/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132194"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132201/selection/dd5d0762a4e76a53598541060c8d37f3eec94419bc3cdca241108e6e27a6201d" :answer/id #uuid "8bba6435-779e-5957-badf-0412b2bca6da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨0,1⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132201/selection/3016f1f84ec843fce16006f5e4e53f53edb0ebd7532c8bb668064aac9885394f" :answer/id #uuid "7cb55de1-7ee1-55fc-8f30-cbc48d421308" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-1,0⟩$ and the radius is $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132201/selection/d328360f5cbfe807f667d67b0ccef89dd88456ac481a34ba3c391ba6900cf321" :answer/id #uuid "eeb1d4a5-3e92-5467-97e5-c72606f1b41a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-1,0⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132201/selection/b36cdb58ee7a0d661a5dbc933d8f7f49976578e2b19c05e9e2015e0a31f396a0" :answer/id #uuid "e8af8469-ed23-56b5-898d-673b0ab10a62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨1,1⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132201/selection/e5e32f617bdcdf1405e176d95594b389d4ac736d8e48b70b03da571c2f63c5bb" :answer/id #uuid "43ba9c72-ee53-5b6c-afa9-225c9763f3ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨0,-1⟩$ and the radius is $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132201/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7107b47-8e6a-5848-98c5-ea5b10956e86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132201/selection/d328360f5cbfe807f667d67b0ccef89dd88456ac481a34ba3c391ba6900cf321" :answer-field/choices ["q-132201/selection/dd5d0762a4e76a53598541060c8d37f3eec94419bc3cdca241108e6e27a6201d" "q-132201/selection/3016f1f84ec843fce16006f5e4e53f53edb0ebd7532c8bb668064aac9885394f" "q-132201/selection/d328360f5cbfe807f667d67b0ccef89dd88456ac481a34ba3c391ba6900cf321" "q-132201/selection/b36cdb58ee7a0d661a5dbc933d8f7f49976578e2b19c05e9e2015e0a31f396a0" "q-132201/selection/e5e32f617bdcdf1405e176d95594b389d4ac736d8e48b70b03da571c2f63c5bb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132201" :question/id #uuid "de6572f6-f3fc-58fb-9ae5-c9150e2f51b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-132201" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,1)$ where $t=0,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖=\\sqrt{2},$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨0,1⟩,$ since the point $P(0,1)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨0,1⟩+\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩+⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132201/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132201"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
